# Cargo grid placement rules

- Implementation: `lib/ships/cargoGridPlacementRules.ts` (ordered `cargoPlacementRules`).
- Consumer: `findSlot` in `lib/ships/cargoGridPlacement.ts` via `resolvePlacementSlotOrder`.
- Add new behavior as a named rule object (`id`, `summary`, `slotOrder`) and append it to `cargoPlacementRules` — do not hardcode one-off axis loops in `findSlot`.
- Logical X remains nose → ramp; “back of bay” is high X (toward gap on the front bay, toward ramp on the rear bay).
- Current rules:
  - `prefer-back-when-full-height` — footprints with `dz >= bay height` scan X descending so full stacks sit at the back and do not wall off the rest of the bay.
